  Pinned source: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. Author:
  parent session <verbatim|hairer-codex-existence-20261111>. Prose:
  <verbatim|manuscript/existence/physical-ward-analytic-continuation.tex>.
  Status: draft, independent mathematical/correspondence review pending.

  <section|Exact interface><label|exact-interface>

  Input S.Hierarchy (including smoothness, translation/permutation/signed
  reflection, positivity), W.Derivatives, SpinRows T, <verbatim|commutes W
  T>, and <verbatim|Collinear W T> at all grades/arities. Output: moment rows
  and their angular finite sum are real analytic along a coordinate motion
  whenever the moving point is strictly first or last in some axis. This
  supplies Ward.channel / stood, and is disjoint from limits agent's Ward
  propagation/commutator/ Outer-price producer file. No full rotation
  representation or global Ward identity is assumed in proving analyticity.

  <section|Focused source correspondence><label|focused-source-correspondence>

  All paths below start <verbatim|Lean/YM/Ward/> at the pin.

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|Plants.lean>: <verbatim|YM.Ward.spot>, <verbatim|link>,
    <verbatim|responds>, <verbatim|blooms>, <verbatim|advancing>. Strong
    derivative via continuous raised-label curve and dense word pairings;
    integrate weak derivative, then identify by density. Normal direction
    uses earlier strictly positive start and OS localHeat, already canonical
    in complex-heat. No claim smoothness implies analyticity.

    <item><verbatim|Genuine.lean>: <verbatim|YM.Ward.pair>, <verbatim|swing>,
    <verbatim|radial>, <verbatim|fires>. Upper insertion first in pair;
    reflected label involution; stationary Gram kernel with difference t-s.
    Exact reflected-label convention retained.

    <item><verbatim|Sum.lean>: <verbatim|YM.Ward.commutes>,
    <verbatim|traverses>; <verbatim|Motion.lean> jet_line (used through
    Rows/Walk; immediate caller inspected). Derivative of angular expression
    equals angular expression on raised label; plus matrix-column term in
    commutator cancels derivative of spatial coefficient.

    <item><verbatim|Rows.lean>: <verbatim|YM.Ward.F>, <verbatim|sigma>,
    <verbatim|realized>: pair at u e_a+z e_b; K=plane b a has vector (-z,u),
    yielding u d_z-z d_u. All transverse angular jets vanish at line from
    Collinear and commutes, not from a presumed global Ward law.

    <item><verbatim|PDE.lean>: <verbatim|YM.PDE.flow_step>, <verbatim|sure>:
    exact commutation d_z^n(Rf)=R d_z^nf-n d_u d_z^(n-1)f; strong induction
    over transverse jets and all pairs, positive u permits division.

    <item><verbatim|Circles.lean>: <verbatim|YM.Ward.Circle.uniform>,
    <verbatim|vector>, <verbatim|htQ>, <verbatim|solves>, <verbatim|pure>:
    analytic finite-dimensional exp(-theta T) comparator; radial
    sqrt(u^2+z^2), arctan(z/u); equal transverse jets only until Hilbert
    factorial argument proves actual analytic trajectory. No Lie
    representation needed for the single-generator exponential.

    <item><verbatim|Ket.lean>: <verbatim|YM.Analysis.represents>,
    <verbatim|bud>, <verbatim|blossoms>; <verbatim|Rate.lean>:
    <verbatim|YM.Analysis.center>, <verbatim|builds>. Stationary Hilbert Gram
    gives squared derivative norm=absolute 2n-th scalar derivative; analytic
    comparator supplies C R^(-2n)(2n)!, binomial coefficient bound gives norm
    factorial estimate uniform on whole line. Prose uses the equivalent
    Banach integral Taylor remainder (elementary FTC iteration), source uses
    mean remainder with an additional harmless exponential reserve.

    <item><verbatim|Extreme.lean>: <verbatim|YM.Ward.higher>,
    <verbatim|last_adv>, <verbatim|first_adv>: separating hyperplane,
    reflected spectator word, permutation, actual signed reflection and
    parameter sign for b=a. Allows spectators tied in normal coordinates.

    <item><verbatim|Walk.lean>: <verbatim|YM.Ward.channel>, <verbatim|stood>:
    finite angular sum analytic; every segment point has a neighborhood,
    sufficient for identity theorem. Global path geometry remains in the
    separate physical-ward-propagation draft.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Canonical reuse and checks><label|canonical-reuse-and-checks>

  Reuse sec:complex-heat for positive-time holomorphy and the already
  constructed reflection-positive chamber. No new external theorem is
  invoked; finite matrix exponential, differentiation and Taylor estimates
  are explained in full. The shared literature search/catalog for the
  canonical heat reconstruction was already consulted; no expensive
  independent literature search was made.

  Focused complete reads of Plants, Genuine, Rows, PDE, Circles, Ket, Rate,
  Extreme, Walk and Axis, plus relevant Sum identities. <verbatim|git diff
  --check> passed. No Lean source edits or fresh build/axiom replay. No claim
  to resolve inherited source audit limitations. LaTeX/render and independent
  review pending.

  <section|Integration validation \V 2026-11-12 11:35
  UTC><label|integration-validation--2026-11-12-1135-utc>

  Bounded independent source and mathematical review is recorded in
  <verbatim|reviews/draft-review.md>; this remains a conditional draft, not
  whole-proof closure. Main LaTeX build succeeds at 821 pages. The phase-grid
  pages were rendered and inspected in the 814-page intermediate;
  local-compiler and analytic pages were rendered and inspected in the
  821-page artifact. See validation.md. No fresh Lean build or axiom replay
  was run.

